  "notes": "Herdr fork preview (wwelder/herdr): agents ask the owner through the feed\n\nSource: def60f2a3edf6140a3a00f29bce6fd38cea11c9d.\n\n- New `herdr feed ask` (API `feed.ask`): an agent's question, given as a card on stdin (`title`, markdown `body`, `actions` and/or `input`, optional `confirm` and `expires`), is written to `~/.config/herdr/feeds/agents/<id>.json` and pushed to the owner's devices as a time-sensitive alert (`feed: <source>/<id>`) that opens the card in HerdrUp. Devices that take needs-input alerts get it; guests never do.\n- The owner's answer (`feed.act`) is typed back into the asking pane as a prompt with `herdr --session <s> agent prompt`. If the agent is gone, the card is closed with an outcome saying why.\n- Guests and federation peers are denied `feed.ask`.\n\nAll five assets were built by the manual Build artifacts workflow (run 42148924559).\n\nUpdate with `herdr update` on the preview channel.",
